          "candidate_line_count": 6,
          "center_error": 12.863,
          "text": "Article 1 In accordance with the Guidance on High­Quality Business Operations of\nthe Joint­Stock Company and the Implementation Rules for High­Quality\nBusiness Operations (Trial) of CCECC (CCECC Operations [2024]341 No.), to\ncomprehensively improve project business quality, effectively manage domestic\nbusiness operations of the company, and standardize business procedures and\nworkflows, these Measures are hereby formulated."
        },
        {
          "page": 2,
          "role": "article_text",
          "source_block": 8,
          "candidate_block": 5,
          "candidate_line_count": 3,
          "center_error": 15.936,
          "text": "Article 2 The projects referred to in these Measures include consulting, survey, design,\nsupervision, general contracting, and other business operations undertaken by the\ncompany through direct commission or bidding."
        },
        {
          "page": 2,
          "role": "article_text",
          "source_block": 10,
          "candidate_block": 6,
          "candidate_line_count": 3,
          "center_error": 33.917,
          "text": "Article 3 In principle, project acquisition work shall follow the procedure of first\nconducting project evaluation, then applying for approval, and finally signing the\ncontract."
        },
        {
          "page": 2,
          "role": "article_text",
          "source_block": 12,
          "candidate_block": 7,
          "candidate_line_count": 8,
          "center_error": 15.947,
          "text": "Article 4 When undertaking project acquisition work, factors such as the\ncompany's development strategy, business direction, responsibility cost,\nproduction and technical capabilities, and current status shall be co\nmprehensively considered. In accordance with the procedures specified in\nthese Measures, the following stages shall be completed: information tracking,\nproject evaluation and application, bid preparation and review, contract\nnegotiation, contract review and signing, owner service during project\nimplementation, and project follow­up visit."
        },
        {
          "page": 2,
          "role": "chapter_heading",
          "source_block": 17,
          "candidate_block": 8,
          "candidate_line_count": 1,
          "center_error": 3.826,
          "text": "Chapter 2 Relevant Responsibilities"
